From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pid: skip host-powered tach failures while host is off

CEB-GNRD fan tach sensors are unavailable with host DC power off. Initialize
the host monitor before creating zones and gate tach failure logging and
timeout checks on a confirmed Host Off state. Keep thermal control and PWM
writes active. Running, transitional and unknown states retain fan checks.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD host-powered fan policy]
---

--- a/hoststatemonitor.hpp
+++ b/hoststatemonitor.hpp
@@ -40,6 +40,12 @@
         return powerStatusOn;
     }
 
+    // Unknown and transitional states must retain failure checks.
+    bool isPowerOff() const
+    {
+        return powerStatusOff;
+    }
+
   private:
     explicit HostStateMonitor(sdbusplus::bus_t& bus);
 
@@ -48,6 +54,7 @@
 
     sdbusplus::bus_t& bus;
     bool powerStatusOn;
+    bool powerStatusOff = false;
     std::unique_ptr<sdbusplus::match> hostStateMatch;
 };
 
@@ -82,6 +89,9 @@
